## Prerequisites

- Terraform installed
- AWS credentials with permission to create the selected EC2/VPC, endpoint, NAT gateway, IAM, and S3 resources
- A Databricks service principal with the Account Admin role ([create and manage service principals](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/admin/users-groups/manage-service-principals))
- Your Databricks account ID
{{#unless create_new_vpc}}
- Existing VPC, at least two private subnets in different Availability Zones, and a workspace security group
{{/unless}}
{{#if enable_private_link}}
{{#unless create_new_vpc}}
- Existing Databricks REST API and SCC relay VPC endpoints in that VPC
{{/unless}}
{{/if}}

## Authenticate

Configure AWS credentials with `aws configure` or your normal AWS CLI/profile process. See [AWS CLI configuration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/cli-chap-configure.html). These AWS credentials are separate from the Databricks credentials below.

Create an OAuth secret for the Databricks service principal by following the [OAuth machine-to-machine authentication guide](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/dev-tools/auth/oauth-m2m), then export its client ID and secret without placing them in `terraform.tfvars`:

```bash
export TF_VAR_databricks_account_id="<your-databricks-account-id>"
export DATABRICKS_CLIENT_ID="<service-principal-client-id>"
export DATABRICKS_CLIENT_SECRET="<service-principal-secret>"
```

Do not commit these values.

## Metastore

This deployment requires a Unity Catalog metastore assignment for the workspace. It creates or attaches the selected metastore. Optional catalog and cluster creation are disabled.

{{#if enable_private_link}}
## Back-end PrivateLink Networking

{{#if create_new_vpc}}
{{#if is_fully_private}}
The fully private network topology creates no NAT gateway or internet gateway. Back-end PrivateLink and the S3, STS, and Kinesis endpoints provide the required private paths for control-plane and AWS service communication.
{{else}}
The standard network topology creates the VPC, {{#if (eq nat_gateway_mode "per_az")}}one NAT gateway per availability zone{{else}}one shared NAT gateway{{/if}}, an internet gateway, workspace subnets, and the required endpoints.
{{/if}}
{{else}}
The custom topology uses the existing VPC, subnet, security group, REST VPC endpoint, and SCC relay VPC endpoint IDs in `terraform.tfvars`. Terraform does not create or modify those existing network resources.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

## Deploy

All Terraform files are at the ZIP root:

```bash
terraform init
terraform fmt -check
terraform validate
terraform plan -var-file=terraform.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=terraform.tfvars
```

Review the plan carefully before applying it.

## Cleanup

```bash
terraform destroy -var-file=terraform.tfvars
```

Destroying infrastructure can permanently remove workspace resources and data.

